  "body_html": "<h1>Convex Coalitional Game</h1>\n<p>A coalitional game is <strong>convex</strong> when its characteristic function is\nsupermodular:\n$$\n  v(S \\cup T) + v(S \\cap T) \\ge v(S) + v(T)\n$$\nfor all coalitions $S,T \\subseteq N$.</p>\n<p>Equivalently, a player's marginal contribution weakly increases as the\ncoalition they join becomes larger. Convexity is a strong regularity\ncondition: convex games have nonempty core, and their Shapley value lies in\nthe core.</p>\n<h2>Lean Status</h2>\n<p>Lean defines convexity as <code>CoalitionalGame.IsConvex</code> and proves the basic\nfact <code>CoalitionalGame.IsConvex.isSuperadditive</code>.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ Ch.17, Def 17.51 and Thm 17.54] Maschler, Solan, Zamir,\n  <em>Game Theory</em>, <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
  "proof_html": null,
